      {
        "review_id": 174765169,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r174765169-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Beautiful grounds to explore, but overpriced tickets for foreigners",
        "text": "This temple is essentially a large park with many buildings, temples and grounds to explore. A river runs through it where you can see bodies being burnt in funerals. Lots of green spaces surround the temple, and you can spend a good part of the day relaxing, strolling, and exploring. You can't enter the temple building if you're not Hindu, as with other Hindu temples, and many signs will remind you of that. The only thing that disappointed me greatly though is the large sum we had to pay to enter the grounds as foreigners. At 1000 rupees per foreigner, it was the highest we have paid in Kathmandu to visit any attraction.\n\nOverall, it is worth a visit, but does have have some drawbacks, including the ticket prices and not having access to the courtyards of the temples at least, which you can peek at through the temple gates. I suggest adding another site to your day after visiting this temple, and one that is nearby which I suggest is the beautiful Boudhanath stupa, which is also surrounded by restaurants and cafes if you wish to take a break or have some lunch.",
